{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591657-a-rules-question-about-dots-and-style","id":591657,"title":"A Rules Question About Dots and Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-15T13:17:24-07:00","id":591657,"title":"A Rules Question About Dots and Style","content":"While selecting Merits for my Demon Character I came across &quot;Terrible Form ( o - oooo , Style).&quot;<br /> <br /> I am interested in the o dot and ooo dot modifications.<br /> <br /> Am I correct that this will cost me oooo Merit dots?<br /> <br /> Do I have to take the oo dot modification before I can access the ooo dot modification?<br /> <br /> What is the &quot;Style&quot; bit?<br /> <br /> Sorry if this is a noob question, but I want to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2651-thlaylie","name":"Thlaylie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:27:59-07:00","id":591693,"title":"","content":"Buying the 0 and 000 would cost 3 merit points total and would require the purchase of the second level in between the style is just a progressing merit 0, 00, 000, 0000 dots grows progressively stronger<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3839-crytofloragardener","name":"CrytofloraGardener","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:32:04-07:00","id":591703,"title":"","content":"Thank You for the info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2651-thlaylie","name":"Thlaylie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:35:24-07:00","id":591708,"title":"","content":"If you want the 3rd dot:<br /> <br /> It will cost you three dots.<br /> <br /> You have to take the 2nd dot before the 3rd dot.<br /> <br /> Style is a keyword tag that has, unfortunately, not been applied quite as well as it should be in the 2e material, which means its definition ends up lacking in clarity. What Style means is, basically, what I posted above. A Style Merit is a Merit that is rating from 1 to X (most are 1 to 5 but some aren't, such as Terrible Form), that it purchased like any other scaled rating Merit (So purchasing Resources 3 costs the same as purchasing Terrible Form 3), but each dot provides a unique mechanical effect, and those effects are acquired in the listed order. The main point of the style tag is that last one, it is not X number of modifications you get to pick from in any order. You have to pick them up in the order listed.<br /> <br /> There are, Merits that work this way, but don't have the Style tag even if they aren't as obviously &quot;styles&quot; in the original sense of the word (the term is derived from Fighting Style Merits in 1e, and 1e eventually added other ____ Style Merits). So it can create confusion as to what the term is supposed to imply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T14:14:05-07:00","id":591771,"title":"","content":"Or in short, &quot;style&quot; is there to clarify that Terrible Form is one Merit you buy up that stacks more benefits as you increase it, rather than a set of five separate but related Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T17:03:23-07:00","id":593365,"title":"","content":"My favorite way to describe Style Merits isn't as a single merit, but as a set of 1-dot merits that must be taken in a row.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T08:14:34-08:00","id":761516,"title":"","content":"So what's the difference between Style merits and merits like Mystery Cult Initiation which have discreet effects per rank but aren't Style merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T14:39:15-08:00","id":761718,"title":"","content":"Nothing; Mystery Cult Initiation behaves like a Style Merit and just isn't labelled as one. Style made more sense as a distinct category in first edition, when it related to how Merit experience costs scaled (a 1 dot Merit and a 2 dot Merit combined didn't have the same cost as one 3 dot Merit). I have the impression Style made more sense in earlier drafts of the 2e rules, but didn't disappear when later drafts rendered it less meaningful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T08:10:53-08:00","id":764065,"title":"","content":"Professional Training is also effectively a Style merit these days.<br /> <br /> Even if Style merits are slightly confusing, I enjoy them a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}